From e81ca094e25a159d0d273cd3cdf515b122db189c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:55:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: the Servo Click, PCA9685 and LTC2497

click-servo answers for both chips: the PCA9685 at 0x40 (All Call,
sub-addresses, the general call's software reset, auto-increment,
RESTART, PRE_SCALE only while asleep, full on and off, INVRT, ALL_LED,
EXTCLK only from sleep) with OE# on the socket's CS, and a minimal
LTC2497 at 0x14 that reads each servo's current through its shunt. The
pulse widths and the servos' angles (by a settable servo law) are
properties for front ends. qtest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
